    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:5acd1ff62dd7566b",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "20bc1fe3e6e86704e9635ef97ecec3268201468626243ff00bd788dd25a992ea",
      "text": "Breakfast. Your sightseeing tour of Cusco begins in the afternoon. The city preserves both Inca structures and Spanish colonial architecture.\n\nFirst, visit Qorikancha, the Temple of the Sun. At this religious centre, the Incas held ceremonies in honour of the sun, including celebrations of the winter solstice.\n\nNext, visit four archaeological sites outside the city. At Sacsayhuamán, see massive walls, terraces and the remains of towers, with enormous stone blocks fitted together with remarkable precision. At Q’enqo, passages, niches and ceremonial areas survive in the rock. Puka Pukara, the “Red Fortress”, is thought to have served defensive and administrative purposes. At Tambomachay, stone channels, terraces and flowing water show how the Incas built structures connected with the worship of water.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw8xmmzc-4ws6bwp2vxe",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:91653954c27b25a7",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "84fc948887503a15e64028db23ea0efb68da48ddb0749f348cf6351f389377de",
      "text": "Before the main sightseeing tour, you can visit Cusco Cathedral, which houses a collection of religious art. The visit takes about 40 minutes and costs an additional $30 per person.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw8xmmzc-4ws6bwp2vxe",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:97d149ee71d1d925",
